  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\int \\frac{x+1}{\\sqrt{2 x-1}} \\mathrm{~d} x=f(x) \\sqrt{2 x-1}+\\mathrm{C},$ where $\\mathrm{C}$ is a constant\r\n\r\nof integration, then $f(x)$ is equal to:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wm2Nw",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{3}(x+1)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "NgSOL",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}(x+2)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "HuPig",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}(x-4)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ERRKY",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{3}(x+4)$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $I=\\int \\frac{x+1}{\\sqrt{2 x-1}} d x$\r\n\r\nPut $\\sqrt{2 x-1}=t$\r\n\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\therefore \\quad 2 x-1=t^{2} \\Rightarrow d x=t d t \\\\\r\n\r\nI=\\int \\frac{\\left(t^{2}+3\\right)}{2} d t=\\frac{t^{3}}{6}+\\frac{3 t}{2}+C \\\\\r\n\r\n=\\frac{(2 x-1)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{6}+\\frac{3}{2}(2 x-1)^{\\frac{1}{2}}+C \\\\\r\n\r\n=\\sqrt{2 x-1}\\left(\\frac{x+4}{3}\\right)+C \\\\\r\n\r\n=f(x) \\cdot \\sqrt{2 x-1}+C\r\n\r\n\\end{array}$\r\n\r\nHence, $f(x)=\\frac{x+4}{3}$",
    "image": null
  },
